---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Container from "@repo/ui/Container.astro";
import { SITE } from "@/data/site";

const lastUpdated = "September 4, 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Privacy Policy | ${SITE.name}`}
  description={`How ${SITE.name} handles your data. In short: nothing you paste or upload ever leaves your browser.`}
  path="/privacy-policy"
>
  <Container>
    <article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl py-14">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-white">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-neutral-500">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <div class="mt-6 space-y-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-neutral-400">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">What you paste or upload</h2>
        <p>
          Every tool on {SITE.name} — the JSON formatter, Base64 encoder, hash generator, regex tester, and JWT
          decoder — processes your input entirely within your browser, using JavaScript's built-in JSON parser, the
          Web Crypto API, and native regular expressions. Text you type, files you drop for Base64 encoding, and
          tokens you paste into the JWT decoder are never transmitted to any server we operate.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">JWT secrets</h2>
        <p>
          If you use the JWT decoder's optional signature-verification feature, the secret you enter is used only to
          run a local HMAC verification in your browser via the Web Crypto API. It is never sent anywhere, and is
          discarded the moment you navigate away or reload the page.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">Analytics</h2>
        <p>
          We may use privacy-respecting analytics to understand aggregate traffic patterns (e.g. which pages are
          visited, approximate country of origin). This data is anonymized/aggregated and is not linked to any
          content you process on this site.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">Advertising</h2>
        <p>
          This site may display advertising served by Google AdSense. Google and its partners may use cookies or
          similar technologies to serve ads based on your prior visits to this or other websites. You can opt out of
          personalized advertising by visiting Google's{" "}
          <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" class="text-accent-400 underline underline-offset-2" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
            Ads Settings
          </a>. For more information on how Google uses data, see{" "}
          <a
            href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites"
            class="text-accent-400 underline underline-offset-2"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            target="_blank"
          >
            How Google uses information from sites that use its services
          </a>.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          This site itself does not set cookies for its tools to function. Third-party services we use (analytics,
          advertising, once enabled) may set their own cookies, governed by their own privacy policies.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Depending on your location, you may have rights under regulations such as the GDPR or CCPA to access,
          correct, or delete personal data we hold about you. Since we do not collect the content you process on this
          site, there is generally nothing of that nature to request. For questions, see our{" "}
          <a href="/contact" class="text-accent-400 underline underline-offset-2">Contact page</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>We may update this policy from time to time. Changes will be posted on this page with an updated revision date.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </Container>
</BaseLayout>
